## Original Content
Graphics: China-SCO trade volume increases over 40-fold in 25 years

## Summary
The trade volume between China and the Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO) has increased over 40 times in the past 25 years, indicating substantial economic growth and strengthened bilateral ties.

## Key Points
- Trade volume between China and SCO increased by more than 40-fold.
- This growth occurred over a 25-year period.
- The increase reflects enhanced economic cooperation and regional integration.
- It highlights China's expanding role in global trade.
- The data may suggest broader geopolitical and economic implications.


